       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults of 200 mg/day. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects. Your patient has normal kidney and liver function and no allergies, so nothing in their profile explains the higher dose.\n\nCould you check whether one of these applies?\n\n- **Typo or unit error:** Did you mean 200 mg, 100 mg, or 40 mg?\n- **Titration:** Standard dosing starts at 25\u201350 mg daily. It goes up in 25\u201350 mg steps at intervals of at least a week, to a maximum of 200 mg/day.\n- **Intentional supratherapeutic dosing:** If this is deliberate, for example on a psychiatry recommendation, tell me and I'll add a note with the rationale. I'd suggest confirming with pharmacy or psychiatry first.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. For example, I can enter sertraline 200 mg PO once daily, or a lower dose if you're starting or titrating."
